                <pb facs="0867" n="741" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg741"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/6248: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Mayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-06-09T09:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 9, 1925—9
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 9—3:46 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>212. My 205, June 6, 4 p.m. The following telegram, 29 hours in transmission, has
                    been received from the consul general at Canton: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“June 7, 5 p.m. Referring to my telegram of June 5, 3 p.m. Fighting began
                            about 4:30 p.m. on Saturday and still continues. All Americans safe so
                            far.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
